-- dead code elimination

```lua
local a = false
if a then
    print(true)
end
```
becomes
```lua
```

```lua
local a = false
local function check()
    if a then
        print(true)
    end
end

a = true
check()
```

should not change

-- new --optimize rule:

typeof is a newer function that supports more types than type, so we can replace type with typeof in some cases.
```lua
if typeof("") == "string" then
end
```
becomes:
```lua
if type("") == "string" then
end
```

type is SLIGHTY faster than typeof because it has less types to check
we can optimize typeof to type for strings, numbers, booleans, tables, threads, and functions, but not for any userdata

the Rule will do other stuff